    "notes": {
        "4b2383ac-8b6b-4ef4-8014-fabbeef67fc6": {
            "x": 480,
            "y": 144,
            "width": 384,
            "height": 400,
            "content": "## ⚠️ Test data assumption\n\nThe triggers create their change stream on flow start, so the table must exist **before** the flow starts. Run once in the account's database (it must be writable, not `SNOWFLAKE`):\n\n```sql\nCREATE TABLE PUBLIC.APPMIXER_E2E_TRIGGERS (ID NUMBER, NAME VARCHAR);\nINSERT INTO PUBLIC.APPMIXER_E2E_TRIGGERS VALUES (1, 'e2e-updated-seed'), (2, 'e2e-new');\n```\n\nEach run deletes the `e2e-new` row left by the previous run (DeletedRow), inserts a new `e2e-new` row for the next run (NewRow) and updates row `ID = 1` (UpdatedRow). A stream only shows the net change, so the deleted and updated rows must exist before the flow starts. That is why there is no cleanup."
        }
    }
